{"name":"Cafe Latte","hex":"#d6c6b4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cafe","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of café.","A convenience store, originally one that sold coffee and similar basic items."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cafe"},{"term":"latte","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A drink of coffee made from espresso and steamed milk, generally topped with foam.","A similar drink, where the espresso is replaced with some other flavoring ingredient such as chai, maté or matcha (green tea)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pillar capped by a hemispherical stone capital with the flat side facing up, used as building supports by the ancient Chamorro people and now used as a sign of Chamorro identity."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/latte"}],"entries":[{"title":"Latte","blocks":[{"text":"Latte or caffè latte, also known as caffellatte, caffelatte, or rarely caffè e latte, is a coffee drink of Italian origin made with espresso coffee and steamed milk, traditionally served in a glass."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Caffe_Latte_at_Pulse_Cafe.jpg/330px-Caffe_Latte_at_Pulse_Cafe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latte"},{"title":"Coffeehouse","blocks":[{"text":"A coffeehouse, coffee shop, or café, is an establishment that serves various types of coffee drinks like espresso, latte, americano and cappuccino, as well as other beverages. An espresso bar specializes in serving espresso and espresso-based drinks. Some coffeehouses may serve iced coffee among other cold drinks, as well as non-caffeinated drinks. A coffeehouse may also serve food, such as light snacks, sandwiches, muffins, cakes, breads, pastries or doughnuts. Many doughnut shops in Canada and the U.S. serve coffee to accompany doughnuts, so these can also be classified as coffee shops, although doughnut shops tend to be more casual and serve cheaper fare. In continental Europe, some cafés even serve alcoholic drinks, and in West Asia, coffeehouses may offer a flavored tobacco smoked through a hookah, called shisha in most varieties of Arabic or nargile in Levantine Arabic, Greek, and Turkish."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Caf%C3%A9_de_Flore.jpg/330px-Caf%C3%A9_de_Flore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coffeehouse"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Coffee_with_milk_%28563800%29.jpg/500px-Coffee_with_milk_%28563800%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Coffee_with_milk_%28563800%29.jpg/1280px-Coffee_with_milk_%28563800%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Coffee_with_milk_%28563800%29.jpg/500px-Coffee_with_milk_%28563800%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Preparation of caffè latte","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACoffee_with_milk_(563800).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Latte_at_Doppio_Ristretto_Chiang_Mai_01.jpg/500px-Latte_at_Doppio_Ristretto_Chiang_Mai_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Latte_at_Doppio_Ristretto_Chiang_Mai_01.jpg/500px-Latte_at_Doppio_Ristretto_Chiang_Mai_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Latte art","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALatte_at_Doppio_Ristretto_Chiang_Mai_01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Palestinian_women_grinding_coffee_beans.jpg/500px-Palestin